---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import releases from "../../data/releases.json";

const latest = releases.releases[0];
const jsonLd = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Organization",
  "name": "TotalRecalls",
  "url": "https://totalrecalls.app",
  "logo": "https://totalrecalls.app/logo.png",
  "description":
    "A Windows app that downloads your AI chat history from ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Qwen Chat into local Markdown + JSON files you own forever.",
});
---
<PageLayout
  title="About TotalRecalls"
  description="TotalRecalls is a Windows app that downloads your AI conversations from 8 providers into local Markdown + JSON files you own. Learn who we are and what we believe."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: "About" }]}
>
  <h1>About TotalRecalls</h1>

  <p>
    TotalRecalls is a small Windows app that downloads your AI conversations from
    <strong>eight providers</strong> — ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini,
    Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral, and Qwen Chat — into plain
    <strong>Markdown + JSON files</strong> on your own computer.
  </p>

  <p>
    Every provider tells you that you own your conversations. When you try to
    actually take them with you, most make you wait days for an download request
    — or hand back only a fraction of what you wrote. TotalRecalls is the
    difference between <em>being told</em> you own your chats and
    <em>actually owning</em> them.
  </p>

  <h2>Why we built it</h2>
  <p>
    Your conversations are years of thinking: decisions, drafts, research, and
    ideas you'll want again. They live inside other companies' accounts, locked
    behind their interfaces. We built TotalRecalls so the archive lands where
    it belongs — in a folder on your PC, in a format you can grep, version,
    back up, and keep forever.
  </p>

  <h2>What we believe</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your chats are yours.</strong> Not ours, and not on a rental plan.</li>
    <li><strong>Local first.</strong> Downloads are written straight to disk. No cloud, no account with us.</li>
    <li><strong>No telemetry.</strong> The app never phones home. Your session tokens stay on your machine.</li>
    <li><strong>One price, no subscription.</strong> $24, one time. No monthly "AI archive" fee.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Supported providers</h2>
  <p>
    ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini (via Google Takeout import), Grok,
    DeepSeek, Mistral, and Qwen Chat. See the
    <a href="/guides/">Guides</a> for per-provider walkthroughs.
  </p>

  <h2>Your data stays yours</h2>
  <p>
    TotalRecalls runs locally on Windows. It never connects to a TotalRecalls
    server, never hosts your chats, and never collects your credentials. You
    can verify this yourself by watching its network traffic. Read the
    <a href="/legals/#privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for the details.
  </p>

  <h2>Pricing & free tier</h2>
  <p>
    TotalRecalls is a one-time <strong>$24 USD</strong> purchase (discounted launch
    price), with no subscription. A <strong>free version</strong> is available now so you
    can test a full download before paying anything — our alternative to a
    refund policy. See the
    <a href="/legals/#pricing">Pricing & Free Tier</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Current version</h2>
  <p>
    The current release is <strong>{latest.tag}</strong> ({latest.date}) —
    {latest.title}. TotalRecalls is a new product and ships updates regularly,
    so this page updates automatically as new versions land.
  </p>
  <h3>What's new in {latest.tag}</h3>
  <ul>
    {latest.changes.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p>Full history lives in the <a href="/release-notes/">Release Notes</a>.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:support@totalrecalls.app">support@totalrecalls.app</a>, or see the
    <a href="/support/">Support</a> page.
  </p>

  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={jsonLd} />
</PageLayout>
